// The article's policy 3, VERBATIM from the published page (the policy text below the plain
// permits), against the article's OWN decision table for it, as `//|` rows. The table is AWS's
// statement of what the policy is for; a row marked `finding` is one where the policy as
// published does the opposite, and both Anchor and the Dogwood engine are held to that.
// Format and harness: tests/policies/agentcore/README.md. Timings are ours where the table's
// are qualitative; input values are ours where the table names none.

// ours: the plain permit the table assumes
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"get_market_price", resource);

// ---- policy 3, verbatim ----
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 30s (
        AgentCore::Action::"get_market_price"::response{eventResource: resource}
    )
};

//| target -
//|
//| row aws-table: 4 seconds ago -- BUY Stock A -- ALLOW
//| @0   request  get_market_price  { stock_symbol: "A", cost: 1000 }  ALLOW ours
//| @1   response get_market_price  { stock_symbol: "A", cost: 1000 } -> { price: 10 }
//| @5    request  execute_trade  { profile_id: "client-1", portfolio_id: "port-8821", cost: 1000 }  ALLOW
//|
//| row aws-table: 2 minutes ago -- BUY Stock A -- DENY
//| @0   request  get_market_price  { stock_symbol: "A", cost: 1000 }  ALLOW ours
//| @1   response get_market_price  { stock_symbol: "A", cost: 1000 } -> { price: 10 }
//| @121  request  execute_trade  { profile_id: "client-1", portfolio_id: "port-8821", cost: 1000 }  DENY
//|
//| row aws-table: Never called -- BUY Stock A -- DENY
//| @0    request  execute_trade  { profile_id: "client-1", portfolio_id: "port-8821", cost: 1000 }  DENY
